      "value": "Franklin H. Littell papers. Subseries 2.1: National Council of Methodist Youth, 1934-1991 (bulk 1936-1941)"
    },
    {
      "controlledVocab": false,
      "controlledVocabList": null,
      "key": "subsea",
      "label": "Subseries Scope and Content",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Subseries 2.1 contains correspondence, printed materials, minutes, reports, and a variety of other records produced or maintained by Franklin Littell, detailing his involvement in the National Council of Methodist Youth (NCMY). Major players in the national peace movement, existing records of the NCMY also document the planning of national conferences, as well as the First International Conference of Christian Youth in Amsterdam in 1939, which Franklin Littell and his wife Harriet attended. Though to a much lesser degree, the NCMY records also reference issues surrounding civil rights and segregation, agricultural workers’ rights, the reunification of the Methodist Church, and interfaith cooperation. There are additional records related to Franklin Littell, the NCMY and other organizations available for research in the Special Collections Research Center. Please review the collection’s online finding aid for more information."
    },
